  _push(`<div${ssrRenderAttrs(_attrs)}><h1 id="points-vectors-and-paths" tabindex="-1">Points, vectors, and paths <a class="header-anchor" href="#points-vectors-and-paths" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Points, vectors, and paths&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Geometry values are the quiet mathematical layer beneath visible diagrams. A <code>Point</code> says <strong>where</strong> something is. A <code>Vector</code> says <strong>which direction and how far</strong>. A <code>PathData</code> says <strong>which route a pen should follow</strong>.</p><p>All core geometry objects are immutable: methods return new values instead of changing the original.</p><div class="info custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Two geometry entry points</p><p>This page covers the compact geometry values available directly in Studio and from <code>math-diagrammer</code>. For the complete analytic engine, import <code>math-diagrammer/geometry</code> and continue to <a href="./geometry-foundations">Geometry foundations</a> and <a href="./segments">Path segments</a>.</p></div><h2 id="points" tabindex="-1">Points <a class="header-anchor" href="#points" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Points&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="point-x-0-y-0-and-new-point-x-0-y-0" tabindex="-1"><code>point(x = 0, y = 0)</code> and <code>new Point(x = 0, y = 0)</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#point-x-0-y-0-and-new-point-x-0-y-0" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;\`point(x = 0, y = 0)\` and \`new Point(x = 0, y = 0)\`&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>In plain language:</strong> stores one exact coordinate.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>x</code></td><td>Horizontal coordinate; positive moves right</td></tr><tr><td><code>y</code></td><td>Vertical coordinate; positive moves down</td></tr></tbody></table>`);
